# This is an EXAMPLE CODEOWNERS file.
# Copy and adapt to your repo: rename to CODEOWNERS (no .example suffix).
# Learn more: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more @owner references.
# Order matters: last match wins in the same file, so put general rules first,
# then override with specific rules.

# Default owners for everything in docs/
/docs/ @team-docs

# Internal docs — engineering owns accuracy
/docs/internal/ @team-engineering

# User docs — product/PM sign-off recommended
/docs/user/ @team-product @team-docs

# Shared content — both teams
/docs/shared/ @team-docs

# Architecture Decision Records — tech lead review
/docs/internal/decisions/ @team-tech-leads

# Runbooks — ops/SRE review
/docs/internal/operations/ @team-sre

# Root README — anyone on the core team
/README.md @team-core
